Behavioral Techniques Behavioral

32
00:01:55,060 --> 00:01:59,060
techniques examine AI systems through
their observable outputs in

33
00:01:59,060 --> 00:02:02,659
response to different inputs. They are
also sometimes called

34
00:02:02,739 --> 00:02:08,020
black box or simply input output
evaluations. This approach

35
00:02:08,020 --> 00:02:10,699
focuses on what a model does rather than
how

36
00:02:10,699 --> 00:02:15,099
it does it internally. Standard Prompting
and Testing the

37
00:02:15,099 --> 00:02:18,479
most basic form of behavioral analysis is
involves presenting

38
00:02:18,479 --> 00:02:22,840
models with predefined inputs and
analyzing their outputs. For

39
00:02:22,840 --> 00:02:26,639
example, when evaluating capabilities, we
might test a model's

40
00:02:26,639 --> 00:02:30,560
coding ability by presenting it with
programming challenges. For

41
00:02:30,560 --> 00:02:34,520
propensity evaluations, we might analyze
its default responses to

42
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:40,960
ethically ambiguous questions. OpenAI's
GPT4 evaluation demonstrates this approach

43
00:02:41,039 --> 00:02:45,879
through systematic testing across various
domains. However, even this

44
00:02:45,879 --> 00:02:49,599
simple technique involves careful
consideration of how questions are

45
00:02:49,599 --> 00:02:54,240
framed, highlighting how most behavioral
techniques exist on a

46
00:02:54,240 --> 00:02:58,159
spectrum from pure observation to active
intervention. What is

47
00:02:58,159 --> 00:03:02,520
Elicitation and Scaffolding? When we say
