Supervised Fine Tuning

113
00:07:09,439 --> 00:07:12,560
While the prompting techniques described
so far are useful,

114
00:07:12,879 --> 00:07:15,920
research consistently shows they often
fail to reveal a

115
00:07:15,920 --> 00:07:20,680
model's full capabilities. Models
frequently possess abilities that remain

116
00:07:20,680 --> 00:07:25,560
dormant during standard prompting
evaluations. For example, some models

117
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:29,160
deliver poorer quality responses when
users present themselves as

118
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:33,480
having less education, suggesting the
issue isn't capability limitation

119
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:38,040
but rather biased expression of existing
capabilities. This is

120
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:41,759
concerning if AIs hide their own
capabilities see the

121
00:07:41,759 --> 00:07:46,439
sections on sandbagging, scheming,
situational awareness, or sabotage
capabilities,

122
00:07:46,920 --> 00:07:49,680
or if AI labs were deliberately trying to
hide

123
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:54,459
capabilities of their LLMs from auditors.
Eliciting capabilities with

124
00:07:54,459 --> 00:07:57,139
fine tuning might have the potential to
avoid such

125
00:07:57,139 --> 00:08:02,379
failures in some circumstances. Supervised
fine tuning offers a

126
00:08:02,379 --> 00:08:06,980
more reliable approach to capability
elicitation. We explained SFT

127
00:08:07,060 --> 00:08:10,259
in the Foundation Models section of our
Capabilities chapter.

128
00:08:10,740 --> 00:08:14,819
Essentially, rather than relying on
elaborate prompting strategies, this

129
00:08:14,819 --> 00:08:18,779
approach modifies the model's weights to
consistently exhibit specific

130
00:08:18,779 --> 00:08:22,939
behaviors or capabilities. To test the
effectiveness of SFT

131
00:08:22,939 --> 00:08:27,660
for eliciting hidden capabilities,
researchers developed password locked
models,

132
00:08:28,139 --> 00:08:31,220
models deliberately trained to perform
well only when a

133
00:08:31,220 --> 00:08:34,100
specific password is present in the prompt
and to

134
00:08:34,100 --> 00:08:38,500
perform poorly otherwise. Their research
demonstrated that SFT can

135
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:42,340
be remarkably sample efficient, often
requiring only a handful

136
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:46,700
of demonstrations to unlock capabilities
that were previously inaccessible

137
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:50,799
through prompting. In these controlled
experiments, models could be

138
00:08:50,799 --> 00:08:53,879
fine tuned with just a few examples and
recover

139
00:08:53,879 --> 00:08:57,919
over 90% of their hidden performance. This
suggests that

140
00:08:57,919 --> 00:09:01,679
fine tuning based approaches might reveal
capabilities that would

141
00:09:01,679 --> 00:09:06,320
remain hidden during even sophisticated
prompting based evaluations. Given

142
00:09:06,320 --> 00:09:09,960
the effectiveness of sft, several AI labs
have begun

143
00:09:09,960 --> 00:09:13,879
incorporating fine tuning based capability
assessment into their safety

144
00:09:13,879 --> 00:09:17,919
evaluation frameworks. At this point, the
