model's internal activations

232
00:15:09,769 --> 00:15:14,450
into simpler, non overlapping components,
separating mixed concepts from

233
00:15:14,450 --> 00:15:18,730
superposition and making them
interpretable to humans. Recent research

234
00:15:18,970 --> 00:15:23,090
suggests neural networks contain organized
feature families that make

235
00:15:23,090 --> 00:15:28,649
this systematic analysis more feasible.
SAEs successfully extracted interpretable

236
00:15:28,649 --> 00:15:32,940
features from models like Claude 3 Sonnet,
revealing features

237
00:15:32,940 --> 00:15:37,620
related to safety relevant behaviors
including deception, sycophancy, and

238
00:15:37,620 --> 00:15:42,580
bias. Anthropic has demonstrated practical
applications of these techniques

239
00:15:42,580 --> 00:15:45,299
in isolating and tracing the thoughts of a
language

240
00:15:45,299 --> 00:15:49,580
model in alignment auditing. These methods
have even identified

241
00:15:49,580 --> 00:15:53,460
models deliberately trained with hidden
objectives by finding features

242
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:55,779
that activate when the model attempts to
game its

243
00:15:55,779 --> 00:16:00,309
training objectives. While promising,
these results remain preliminary and

244
00:16:00,309 --> 00:16:02,629
have not yet been applied to full scale AI

245
00:16:02,629 --> 00:16:07,190
auditing. At this point, the textbook
shows figure 599.

246
