358
00:22:57,569 --> 00:23:01,329
feature activity. CE is not the only
internal technique

359
00:23:01,329 --> 00:23:04,648
that can be used to detect alignment
faking. Some

360
00:23:04,648 --> 00:23:09,410
researchers have proposed benchmarks to
evaluate interpretability techniques
themselves.

361
00:23:10,289 --> 00:23:14,170
Think about it like evaluating evaluation
techniques. They are

362
00:23:14,170 --> 00:23:17,529
trying to measure the efficacy efficacy of
evaluations in

363
00:23:17,529 --> 00:23:21,220
detecting things like alignment faking.
This is basically the

364
00:23:21,220 --> 00:23:24,579
same thing as scheming, where models
behave benign during

365
00:23:24,579 --> 00:23:27,819
evaluations but misbehave when they infer
it's safe to

366
00:23:27,819 --> 00:23:30,660
do so. An example of this type of
benchmark

367
00:23:30,660 --> 00:23:35,619
is the poser benchmark. The benchmark
comprises 324 pairs

368
00:23:35,619 --> 00:23:39,660
of Llama 13B models fine tuned for
roleplay scenarios.

369
00:23:40,380 --> 00:23:43,460
One model in each pair is consistently
aligned while

370
00:23:43,460 --> 00:23:46,259
the other is an alignment faker that
misbehaves when

371
00:23:46,259 --> 00:23:49,380
it believes it won't be caught. When the
model

372
00:23:49,380 --> 00:23:53,220
is told that monitoring is compromised,
the core task

373
00:23:53,220 --> 00:23:56,299
is to identify the alignment faking model
using only

374
00:23:56,299 --> 00:24:00,460
prompts where both models produce
identical outputs, thus necessitating

375
00:24:00,460 --> 00:24:03,700
the use of internal model analysis rather
than behavioral

376
00:24:03,700 --> 00:24:08,220
differences. The researchers tested five
detection strategies based on

377
00:24:08,220 --> 00:24:12,619
manipulating or observing model internals.
The most successful strategy,

378
00:24:12,700 --> 00:24:16,859
termed intoxicating models by injecting
noise into their activations,

379
00:24:17,259 --> 00:24:21,619
identified 98% of alignment fakers. This
was done by

380
00:24:21,619 --> 00:24:26,059
observing which model shifted more towards
misaligned outputs. Another

381
00:24:26,059 --> 00:24:29,980
effective method, comparing how quickly
models learn to misbehave

382
00:24:30,220 --> 00:24:34,220
by fine tuning them towards misaligned
actions, achieved 90%

383
00:24:34,220 --> 00:24:39,579
accuracy. With fakers adapting more
rapidly, identifying suspicious concepts

384
00:24:39,579 --> 00:24:43,650
like security or harmful behavior use
using activation directions

385
00:24:43,650 --> 00:24:48,769
yielded 71% accuracy. Conversely,
strategies like trying to induce

386
00:24:48,769 --> 00:24:51,569
a belief that it's safe to misbehave,
which was

387
00:24:51,569 --> 00:24:56,130
indistinguishable from noise injection,
comparing decision making speed across

388
00:24:56,130 --> 00:24:59,650
layers or measuring attentiveness to
oversight cues were not

389
00:24:59,650 --> 00:25:03,410
effective. While interpretability is a
valuable tool, it is

390
00:25:03,410 --> 00:25:07,329
unlikely to provide highly reliable
methods for detecting sophisticated

391
00:25:07,329 --> 00:25:11,890
scheming. There are many fundamental
challenges to interpretability like

392
00:25:11,890 --> 00:25:16,849
superposition where concepts are
distributed across neurons, inherent
errors

393
00:25:16,849 --> 00:25:20,650
in current tools like SAEs, difficulty in
measuring progress

394
00:25:20,650 --> 00:25:24,369
without ground truth, the long tail
problem of complex

395
00:25:24,369 --> 00:25:27,730
and poorly understood model behaviors, and
the immense difficulty

396
00:25:27,730 --> 00:25:31,769
of proving the absence of deceptive
circuits. Furthermore, issues

397
00:25:31,769 --> 00:25:35,450
like scalability to superintelligent
systems and the potential for

398
00:25:35,450 --> 00:25:39,390
AI to deliberately obfuscate its internal
workings pose significant

399
00:25:39,549 --> 00:25:42,950
hurdles. Internal techniques should be
considered part of a

400
00:25:42,950 --> 00:25:47,269
pragmatic defense in depth portfolio of
safeguards. The aim

401
00:25:47,269 --> 00:25:49,390
of these should be to maximize the chances
of

402
00:25:49,390 --> 00:25:54,309
catching misalignment rather than
guaranteeing its detection.
Interpretability should

403
00:25:54,309 --> 00:25:56,349
be thought of as a complement to black box

404
00:25:56,349 --> 00:26:02,349
methods by providing de correlated
signals, enhancing evaluations by

405
00:26:02,349 --> 00:26:05,849
manipulating a model's awareness of being
tested, and helping

406
00:26:05,849 --> 00:26:10,130
to debug mysterious or concerning model
behaviors. The goal

407
00:26:10,130 --> 00:26:12,650
should be to make deception harder and
riskier for

408
00:26:12,650 --> 00:26:16,769
AI, even if perfect detection remains
elusive. Much more

409
00:26:16,769 --> 00:26:20,009
details on interpretability can be found
in the dedicated

410
00:26:20,009 --> 00:26:21,409
chapter on Interpretability.
